{sec("", f"""{split("01", f"Cross border.<br>Not cross settle{G}", "In a shared omnibus account, securities received for one client&rsquo;s buy can be used to meet an unrelated client&rsquo;s sell. That is cross settlement. For larger clients, where volumes justify it, EMFI can arrange individually segregated securities accounts at Euroclear, within its direct participant infrastructure.")}<div class="mt rv" style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:28px;padding:clamp(16px,3vw,36px)">{omni}</div><div class="split mt" style="align-items:start"><p class="rv">Cross border also works the other way. Where the security, route and counterparty allow, EMFI can settle across depositories: a seller delivering through DTC while a buyer receives through Euroclear. Charges may apply.</p><p class="fine rv">Dedicated accounts depend on eligibility, account configuration and commercial terms. Segregation helps identify your assets and reduces certain cross-client risks. It does not remove market, depository, counterparty, banking or insolvency risk. {T("Confirm Euroclear participant status, account eligibility and supported cross-depository routes")}</p></div>""")}
{sec("navy", f"""{split("02", f"Mind the<br>(settlement) gap{G}", "When your buy settles but the sell that funds it fails, you are left financing the position and paying interest while you wait. EMFI links the two instructions so the buy is held back if the sell is not ready to settle, helping you avoid the interim financing and the interest that comes with it. Other fail charges, such as CSDR penalties and TMPG fails charges, may still apply and are passed through where applicable. Where the information is available we automate their capture and give you the references to review and dispute them with your counterparties.")}<div class="mt rv">{gap}</div><p class="fine" style="margin-top:12px">CSDR penalties are statutory. TMPG fails charges are a market-practice charge. {T("Confirm linked-trade functionality and conditions with Operations")}</p>""")}
